# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# <body>
#
# <footer>

# --- COMMIT END ---
# Type can be:
#  build    (changes that affect the build system or external dependencies)
#  chore    (routine maintenance that does not change production behavior)
#  ci       (changes to CI configuration files and scripts)
#  docs     (changes to documentation)
#  feat     (new user-facing feature)
#  fix      (fix addressing a user bug)
#  perf     (performance-related change)
#  refactor (refactoring production code)
#  revert   (reversion in code)
#  style    (formatting changes - no production code logic changes)
#  test     (adding or refactoring tests - no production code changes)
#
# Scope is optional and is intended for specifying a granular context appropriate for the changes.
#
# Common scopes used for this project:
# admin, deps, docs, harden, release, runtime, scanner, ui
#
# Subject should use imperative mood and say what you did.
# The body should go into detail about changes made.
# The footer should contain any related or resolved GitHub issue keys.
#
# For a full example:
#   feat(lang): add Gibberish language support
#
#   Added support for Gibberish language including:
#   - New language files
#   - Translation updates
#   - Unit tests for language switching
#
#   Refs:
#   - #1234
#   - #1235
